  "notes": [
    "Input pipeline is a TAKEOVER control macro including its embedded wait/assert steps. Standalone Wait/Assert remains READ-compatible.",
    "Arm management, cancellation and explicit mode/Lease management are mode-independent but retain their scopes and credentials.",
    "Recording observation and Artifact IO are READ-compatible; they are not Persistent Write.",
    "Persistent Read is READ-compatible in native HTTP; the current curated MCP tool set has no dedicated Persistent Read tool.",
    "Peer queries/probe are READ-compatible. Existing typed Peer Fixture/Debug requests enter through OPERATE-gated client Runtime workflows and retain independent server operator/feature gates. Mode is not a remote-server authentication credential.",
    "Ordinary pooled HTTP disconnect does not change stable intent. Lease-bound control WS disconnect/TTL loss ends TAKEOVER. Runtime close ends its entire control session.",
    "No mode automatically upgrades scopes, obtains a Debug Arm, or turns Fixture/Debug evidence into PLAYTEST."
  ]
}
